#: ../../source/docs/common-djirs2-gimbal.rst:55
#: e3476d11659947b08358ce0e208d0e86
msgid "Yaw rate control is always \"follow\" mode (aka \"earth frame\") meaning that if the user control the gimbal's yaw rotation rate from the RC (e.g. :ref:`MNT1_RC_RATE<MNT1_RC_RATE>` > 0) the gimbal will rotate in \"lock\" mode (e.g. \"earth frame\", e.g. will not rotate with the vehicle). A workaround is to always use yaw angle control (e.g. :ref:`MNT1_RC_RATE<MNT1_RC_RATE>` = 0) or switch the mount to \"Neutral\" whenever the user wishes to re-center it."
msgstr ""

